-- Passage wg11-narrative-writing-p02
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('323f5b14-65ea-5553-9c2c-4a53693e5ffc', 'wg11-narrative-writing-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-narrative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Nineteen Miles North$q$, $q$(1) Our physics class had spent a month building a payload box out of foam and tape, and on a cold March morning we finally released our weather balloon from the soccer field. (2) Inside the box were a small camera, a temperature sensor, and a tracker that would report the box's location once it fell back to earth. (3) Ms. Adeyemi-Clarke counted down from ten, and the white balloon rose so fast that within a minute it was only a dot against the clouds.

(4) The tracker updated every five minutes on Tomas's laptop. (5) We followed the dots north as the balloon drifted over farms, a reservoir, and finally a long ridge of pine forest. (6) Then the dots stopped. (7) "Maybe it's still climbing out of range," Tomas said, not sounding convinced.

(8) We drove toward the last location, ate lunch, and waited. (9) Two hours later, the laptop chimed. (10) The box had landed in an orchard nineteen miles away, and the signal was strong.

(11) The farmer who owned the orchard, a tall woman named Ruth Lindqvist, met us at her gate. (12) She had already found the box tangled in the branches of an apple tree. (13) "I thought somebody's science project had escaped," she said, handing it over with a grin.

(14) That night, we watched the footage in the classroom. (15) The camera showed the curve of the earth, a thin blue band of atmosphere, and then a black sky. (16) Some apple trees produce fruit for more than fifty years.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
