   $q$Which revision of sentence 8 best signals the shift in time and setting from the dock to the race?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The race started, and it was a race on the river.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"redundant-no-transition"},{"text":"The race started, just like every other race we had ever rowed in before.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"deflates-tension"},{"text":"An hour later, the mist had thinned, and we sat at the starting line beside five other boats, waiting for the horn.","is_correct":true},{"text":"However, the race started after that.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contrast-not-time"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$An hour later, the mist had thinned, and we sat at the starting line beside five other boats, waiting for the horn.$q$, $q$"An hour later" marks the time shift, and the starting line with other boats shows the new setting and builds anticipation. "However" signals a contrast that does not exist.$q$, 'draft', '2467747a-cf2a-53b6-97a6-bd364b396dca')
