   $q$Which sentence, added after sentence 4, would best establish the narrator's point of view going into the experience?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The nature center has walking trails, a pond, and a small museum about local wildlife.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"setting-not-pov"},{"text":"I had read about the migration for years, but I had never touched a monarch, and I worried I would hurt one.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Monarchs travel thousands of miles each fall to spend the winter in warmer places.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"fact-not-pov"},{"text":"Dr. Siddiqui has been tagging butterflies for many years and has published several papers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"focuses-on-wrong-character"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$I had read about the migration for years, but I had never touched a monarch, and I worried I would hurt one.$q$, $q$The correct choice shows the narrator's eagerness and fear, which shape how the reader feels when the narrator later holds the butterfly. The other choices give facts about the place, the insect or the scientist instead of the narrator.$q$, 'draft', 'ce1c39f0-3b8d-5408-9e55-8e95fc81e268')
