   $q$What is the effect of the time markers in sentences 5 and 6?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They signal a flashback to the narrator's first day of training at the store.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"false-flashback"},{"text":"They show that the narrator is bored and keeps checking the clock during the shift.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They speed up the pacing and show supplies vanishing, building pressure before Emeka arrives.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They slow the narrative down so the reader can picture every customer in the line.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-pacing-speed"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They speed up the pacing and show supplies vanishing, building pressure before Emeka arrives.$q$, $q$Two quick, parallel sentences with clock times move the story along and show the store emptying, which makes Emeka's request harder to meet. Nothing suggests boredom; the store is busy.$q$, 'draft', '0263af8c-9911-59cf-b483-df6aaced16f9')
