   $q$How do sentences 8 through 10 contribute to the narrative?$q$, $q$[{"text":"They show that the narrator's mother disapproves of the driving lessons.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"They interrupt the story with an unrelated memory and should be removed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-connection"},{"text":"They add a second plot line linking the narrator's struggle to the mother's, echoing sentence 3.","is_correct":true},{"text":"They move the story ahead to the day the narrator passes the driving test.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-sequence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$They add a second plot line linking the narrator's struggle to the mother's, echoing sentence 3.$q$, $q$The mother's own stalling story connects back to "Your mother learned in this truck" and shows struggle is part of a family pattern. Her laughter is affectionate, not disapproving, and the story is about her own lessons.$q$, 'draft', '14f45f66-490f-575b-9b5b-685ec761fe27')
