  ('3fc4ceb9-378a-53c0-9711-8f8fee1cf2bc', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-narrative-writing'), null, 'medium',
   $q$What does sentence 15 suggest about the grandmother?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She is still nervous about letting the narrator drive her truck.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She is bored with the lesson and wants to go home as soon as possible.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-gesture"},{"text":"She shows approval and trust through relaxed body language instead of words.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She is too hot and needs fresh air from the open window.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She shows approval and trust through relaxed body language instead of words.$q$, $q$The writer says she sits this way "when she is driving herself," so the gesture shows she is as comfortable with the narrator driving as with driving herself. Reading it as simply needing air ignores that comparison.$q$, 'draft', '14f45f66-490f-575b-9b5b-685ec761fe27')
