   $q$A reviewer suggests moving sentence 12 so that it opens the third paragraph. Why would this change weaken the passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sentence 12 contains the passage's only transition word, so moving it would leave the paragraphs unconnected.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-claim"},{"text":"Sentence 12 introduces the parity bit, so it must come before sentence 5.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-sentence-content"},{"text":"Sentence 12 sums up the importance of the codes, so moving it would split \"this limitation\" from sentence 7 and leave the passage without a conclusion.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Sentence 12 describes a problem with error-correcting codes, so it should come after the solution.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-sentence-content"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sentence 12 sums up the importance of the codes, so moving it would split "this limitation" from sentence 7 and leave the passage without a conclusion.$q$, $q$Sentence 12 is a broad concluding statement, and sentence 9 must follow the second paragraph directly so that "this limitation" clearly refers to sentence 7. The claim that sentence 12 holds the only transition is false, since words like "then" and "More sophisticated" also link ideas.$q$, 'draft', '387933c9-eda9-5abe-b3cd-1da3644a93d9')
