   $q$Read the sentences: (A) As a result, some birds in cities now sing at a higher pitch than members of the same species in the countryside. (B) Traffic and machinery produce a constant, low rumble in most cities. (C) This background noise can drown out birdsong that falls in the same low range. (D) Researchers suspect that the higher pitch helps the songs carry above the noise. Which is the most logical order?$q$, $q$[{"text":"B, C, A, D","is_correct":true},{"text":"C, B, D, A","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-reference-words"},{"text":"B, A, C, D","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignores-reference-words"},{"text":"A, B, C, D","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"effect-before-cause"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$B, C, A, D$q$, $q$B introduces the noise, C ("This background noise") explains its effect on song, A ("As a result") gives the birds' response, and D explains why the response helps. Order A, B, C, D fails because "As a result" cannot open the paragraph before any cause is given.$q$, 'draft', null)
