   $q$Jamal is writing to the city transit office: "Hey, the number 9 bus is always super late and it's annoying." Which revision best fits a formal letter?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The number 9 bus is never on time, ever, period.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-overstatement"},{"text":"The number 9 bus frequently runs late, which is frustrating.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The number 9 bus is always super late, which really bugs me.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-word"},{"text":"Hey there, the number 9 bus runs late a ton and it's annoying.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-greeting"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The number 9 bus frequently runs late, which is frustrating.$q$, $q$The correct choice keeps the complaint but uses "frequently" and "frustrating" instead of slang. "Never on time, ever, period" sounds like casual speech and exaggerates.$q$, 'draft', null)
