   $q$Read the sentence: "Due to the fact that the river flooded, the rowing race was canceled." Which revision is the most concise?$q$, $q$[{"text":"In light of the fact that the river flooded, the rowing race was canceled.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wordy-phrase"},{"text":"Because the river flooded, the rowing race was canceled.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Owing to the fact that the river flooded, the rowing race was canceled.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wordy-phrase"},{"text":"Although the river flooded, the rowing race was canceled.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-relationship"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because the river flooded, the rowing race was canceled.$q$, $q$"Because" says in one word what "due to the fact that" says in five. "Although" is short too, but it signals contrast, not cause.$q$, 'draft', null)
