   $q$A sentence in a research paper reads: "Coral bleaching is a total disaster for reef fish." Which revision best fits the formal tone of a research paper?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Coral bleaching is a huge bummer for reef fish.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"slang"},{"text":"Coral bleaching is really, really bad for reef fish.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-intensifier"},{"text":"Coral bleaching severely harms reef fish.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Coral bleaching is, honestly, a disaster for reef fish.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-aside"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Coral bleaching severely harms reef fish.$q$, $q$"Severely harms" states the strong effect in measured, formal language. "Really, really bad" keeps the meaning but relies on casual repetition.$q$, 'draft', null)
