   $q$Read the sentences: "The storm passed. The hikers left the shelter. They continued toward the summit." Which revision combines them most smoothly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The hikers continued toward the summit, the storm passed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"changes-order"},{"text":"After the storm passed, the hikers left the shelter and continued toward the summit.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The storm passed, the hikers left the shelter, they continued toward the summit.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-splice"},{"text":"The storm passed and the hikers left the shelter and they continued toward the summit.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"stringy-and"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$After the storm passed, the hikers left the shelter and continued toward the summit.$q$, $q$Opening with "After the storm passed" shows the time order and joins the actions without repetition. The version with three "and"s combines them but reads as a run-on chain.$q$, 'draft', null)
