  ('31b42b28-9c91-5b99-9ffe-dddc5759cb02', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-precise-language'), null, 'medium',
   $q$A report on a regional chess tournament reads: "The brilliant Kwame Asante crushed his pathetic opponents in every round." Which revision keeps an objective tone?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Kwame Asante won every round of the tournament.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Kwame Asante easily crushed his opponents in every round.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"loaded-verb"},{"text":"The brilliant Kwame Asante won every round of the tournament.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"biased-word"},{"text":"Kwame Asante defeated his weak opponents in every round.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"biased-word"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Kwame Asante won every round of the tournament.$q$, $q$The correct choice reports the result without praising or insulting anyone. "The brilliant Kwame Asante won every round" drops "pathetic" but keeps the judgment "brilliant."$q$, 'draft', null)
