  ('a86f655d-7e18-5f7c-9831-09fdcedde398', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-precise-language'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Read the paragraph: "(1) Migratory songbirds rely on stopover habitats to rest and refuel. (2) These patches of forest and shrubland are shrinking as development expands. (3) Honestly, it's kind of a mess for the birds. (4) Several conservation groups have begun purchasing land along major flyways." Which revision of sentence 3 best matches the tone of the paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"This loss is a tragedy that should outrage every reader.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"loses-objectivity"},{"text":"Honestly, this loss poses a serious problem for the birds.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-aside-remains"},{"text":"This loss poses a serious problem for the birds.","is_correct":true},{"text":"This loss is kind of a serious problem for the birds.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"informal-hedge"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$This loss poses a serious problem for the birds.$q$, $q$The correct choice states the problem in the same calm, informational voice as sentences 1, 2, and 4. "A tragedy that should outrage every reader" is formal in vocabulary but turns emotional and breaks the objective tone.$q$, 'draft', null)
