   $q$Which sentence should the writer delete because it does not support the analysis?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Sentence 10, because the age of one oak says nothing about how lichens reflect air quality.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Sentence 7, because percentages make the paragraph harder to read.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-key-evidence"},{"text":"Sentence 9, because it explains evidence instead of giving new facts.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-analysis"},{"text":"Sentence 4, because a direct quotation from the article repeats what sentence 3 says.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"removes-key-evidence"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Sentence 10, because the age of one oak says nothing about how lichens reflect air quality.$q$, $q$Sentence 10 adds a fact about a tree's age that has no link to pollution or lichens. Sentence 9 is the writer's explanation of why the bus route evidence matters, which is exactly what an evidence-based response needs.$q$, 'draft', '27392148-b5b7-5528-9db6-194b6a6c773f')
