   $q$Which detail from Adjei's essay, added after sentence 3, would best support the claim in sentence 2?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Adjei notes that the Merrow Canal was more than ninety miles long when it first opened.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"},{"text":"Adjei notes that one of the founders had been born in a large city far from the canal.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"Adjei notes that the founders moved the start of class to seven o'clock after crews said they could not arrive by six.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Adjei notes that the schoolhouse was built of gray stone taken from a quarry near the canal.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Adjei notes that the founders moved the start of class to seven o'clock after crews said they could not arrive by six.$q$, $q$Changing the class time because of the crews' schedules is direct evidence that the founders adjusted the school to the workers' lives. The building's stone has no connection to that claim.$q$, 'draft', '61903b11-9d54-544c-a03c-0167e95daf4a')
