   $q$Which quotation from the story, added after sentence 6, would best strengthen the second paragraph?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"She counted the passengers twice before untying the rope, the way her grandfather always had.\"","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"The water by the dock was green and full of floating willow leaves.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"description-not-relevant"},{"text":"\"Her friends waved from the beach as the ferry slid past the point.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"},{"text":"\"The ferry's engine was older than Marisol's father and twice as loud.\"","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"description-not-relevant"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"She counted the passengers twice before untying the rope, the way her grandfather always had."$q$, $q$Counting the passengers twice is another careful act that shows Marisol taking responsibility, which is the paragraph's point. The description of the water sets a scene but says nothing about how Marisol has changed.$q$, 'draft', '57329ddd-a95d-5346-b2ef-98b651da1a8b')
