   $q$Which sentence best fills the blank in sentence 5 by explaining the evidence in sentences 3 and 4?$q$, $q$[{"text":"This gap suggests that riders at stops without screens were simply less honest in the survey.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"This gap suggests that knowing when the bus will arrive makes the same nine minutes feel far shorter to riders.","is_correct":true},{"text":"This gap suggests that buses arrived much more often at the stops that had arrival-time screens.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-evidence"},{"text":"This survey was given to riders at many different bus stops across the city of Brennick.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"summary-not-analysis"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$This gap suggests that knowing when the bus will arrive makes the same nine minutes feel far shorter to riders.$q$, $q$Actual waits were the same, but riders with screens felt they waited less, which supports Haddad's claim about perceived waiting. The choice saying buses came more often contradicts sentence 3.$q$, 'draft', '552c5a16-ea51-552f-9486-690415890400')
