-- Passage wg11-writing-with-evidence-p05
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('fcd2195f-c892-56b6-86ef-ca3a8f145083', 'wg11-writing-with-evidence-p05', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g11-writing-with-evidence'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Draft: Why Halvern Keeps Its Rowers$q$, $q$(1) For my research paper, I investigated why the Halvern Rowing Club keeps far more of its first-year rowers than other clubs in the region. (2) I used three sources: a club report by coach Tavita Leaupepe, a regional survey of rowing clubs by researcher Daniel Abebe, and interviews I conducted with four current rowers. (3) Leaupepe's report says the club pairs every new rower with an experienced partner for the first season. (4) Leaupepe's report also says new rowers stay because the club lets them choose morning or evening practices. (5) Leaupepe's report adds that the club "never cuts a beginner for being slow." (6) According to Leaupepe's report, these policies are the reason 81 percent of new rowers return for a second year.

(7) Abebe's survey of twenty clubs found that the average return rate for new rowers is 46 percent. (8) His survey also found that clubs with flexible practice times kept more new rowers than clubs with a single fixed schedule. (9) Three of the four rowers I interviewed said that their partner was the main reason they came back. (10) One rower, Seo-yeon Park, said she nearly quit after tipping her boat in her first week but stayed because her partner "made it feel like a normal part of learning."

(11) ____$q$, 'draft')
