   $q$Which revision of sentence 9 best explains how the quotation in sentence 8 supports the claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"By noting that the cracked bowl still \"rang,\" the speaker values it for what it can still do, accepting what the fire decided.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The speaker finds a cracked bowl when she finally opens the door of the kiln in the morning.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"summary-not-analysis"},{"text":"The speaker will most likely throw the cracked bowl away and start the whole process over.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-evidence"},{"text":"Cracked bowls usually happen when a kiln heats up or cools down too quickly.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-topic-fact"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$By noting that the cracked bowl still "rang," the speaker values it for what it can still do, accepting what the fire decided.$q$, $q$The choice about the cracked bowl that still "rang" connects that word to the speaker's acceptance, which is the draft's claim. Saying she will throw the bowl away contradicts the admiring tone of the quoted line.$q$, 'draft', '86a82509-8375-5c02-b9c8-606fc16ffac7')
