insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('c7f9829b-1780-5ee6-8676-7632991edbf2', 'wg12-argument-writing-p01', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Letting the Roadsides Bloom$q$, $q$(1) Halvorsen County mows the grassy shoulders of its rural roads four times each summer, a schedule that cuts down milkweed, clover and aster before most of them can bloom. (2) Mowing is something that happens in a lot of places. (3) A two-year trial run by the county extension office on eleven miles of Route 9 found that shoulders mowed only once, in late September, supported nearly three times as many pollinating insects as shoulders mowed on the regular schedule. (4) The same trial recorded a 31 percent drop in fuel and labor costs on the test miles. (5) The county's first mowing machine was purchased in 1952 and is now displayed at the fairgrounds.

(6) Road safety officials have raised a fair objection: tall vegetation near intersections and curves can block a driver's view of oncoming traffic. (7) This concern deserves a serious answer, because no benefit to insects would justify a higher risk of collisions. (8) The trial plan kept a six-foot strip beside the pavement, along with the full sight area at every intersection, mowed on the regular schedule. (9) During the trial, the sheriff's office reported no change in the number of crashes on the test miles.

(10) Delayed mowing is basically a no-brainer. (11) Everyone should care about bugs.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
where public.passages.status = 'draft';
