  ('ea50cf5c-a58f-546f-b148-ea18ee4e1eed', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-argument-writing'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Which choice would best replace sentences (10) and (11) as a conclusion that follows from the argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Because the trial increased pollinators and cut costs without raising crash rates, the county should extend late-season mowing to all of its rural roads.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The county should also plant flower gardens in every town park to help insects even more.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"Anyone who still wants four mowings a summer simply has not looked at the facts.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dismissive-tone"},{"text":"In conclusion, roads are important, and the county should always put drivers first.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because the trial increased pollinators and cut costs without raising crash rates, the county should extend late-season mowing to all of its rural roads.$q$, $q$The correct conclusion restates the claim and draws together the three findings the essay presents: more pollinators, lower costs and no change in crashes. Proposing park gardens introduces a new idea instead of concluding the argument.$q$, 'draft', 'c7f9829b-1780-5ee6-8676-7632991edbf2')
