insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('24233b5d-ff09-5478-9b65-8360200f0e4d', 'wg12-argument-writing-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Internship Credit at Brightwater High$q$, $q$(1) Brightwater High requires every senior to complete six elective credits, but it offers no way to earn any of them outside the school building. (2) The school should allow seniors to earn one elective credit through a supervised semester internship with a local employer or nonprofit. (3) At Carver Ridge High, a nearby school that adopted a similar policy five years ago, 68 percent of interns reported that the experience helped them choose a college major or training program. (4) Internships teach habits that classrooms rarely require, such as answering to a supervisor, managing a commute and solving problems alongside adults who are not teachers. (5) I think internships are really fun and everyone would love them.

(6) Some teachers worry that students will treat the internship as an easy credit and learn little. (7) The worry is understandable, since a poorly designed program could become a semester of filing papers. (8) Brightwater could prevent this by requiring a weekly reflection journal, a midterm visit from a faculty advisor and a final presentation graded against a published rubric. (9) Carver Ridge uses these same requirements, and in five years its advisors removed only three placements for lack of meaningful work.

(10) Internships are common in many countries around the world.$q$, 'draft')
