   $q$Which revision of sentence (5) best maintains a formal style and connects to the claim?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Internships can be enjoyable, and enjoyment is something everyone deserves.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-reasoning"},{"text":"Honestly, internships are awesome, and pretty much every senior would want one.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"keeps-informal-tone"},{"text":"Because these skills carry directly into college and work, an internship would serve students as well as many traditional electives do.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Students who prefer classrooms are free to ignore internships if they want.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-point"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because these skills carry directly into college and work, an internship would serve students as well as many traditional electives do.$q$, $q$The correct revision uses formal wording and explains why the skills in sentence (4) justify the credit. The choice about enjoyment is less slangy but still offers feeling instead of reasoning.$q$, 'draft', '24233b5d-ff09-5478-9b65-8360200f0e4d')
