insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('ae69533e-3a40-5e0c-9356-b6792fac88eb', 'wg12-argument-writing-p03', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$Opening the Pellam Mill Ledgers$q$, $q$(1) In the basement of the Pellam Historical Society sit forty-two leather ledgers recording the wages, purchases and hours of workers at the Pellam Woolen Mill between 1861 and 1904. (2) Because the handwriting is faded and impossible to search, almost no researcher has used them in the past decade. (3) The society has applied three times for a state grant to hire a professional transcriber and has been turned down each time. (4) Rather than wait for a fourth attempt, the society should invite trained volunteers to transcribe the ledgers through a shared online platform. (5) The Dorsey County Archive used this approach for its ship registers and finished 6,000 pages in eighteen months, a task its staff had estimated would take a single professional seven years. (6) Volunteer projects also build public interest in local history.

(7) Some archivists caution that volunteers make more errors than professionals, and a careless transcription could mislead future researchers. (8) Those people are just being snobs about who gets to touch old books. (9) Dorsey County had every page transcribed independently by two volunteers, and a staff member reviewed any line where the two versions disagreed. (10) An audit of 500 randomly chosen pages found an error rate below one percent, close to the rate expected from a single professional.

(11) The ledgers have waited long enough.$q$, 'draft')
