   $q$Which choice best explains why the writer should keep sentence (7)?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It provides the main evidence that volunteers can finish the work faster than staff.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-function"},{"text":"It shows that the writer agrees the ledgers should remain untranscribed.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"concession-as-reversal"},{"text":"It states a reasonable opposing claim that sentences (9) and (10) then answer with evidence.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It adds variety by switching to a new topic before the conclusion.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-structure"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It states a reasonable opposing claim that sentences (9) and (10) then answer with evidence.$q$, $q$Sentence (7) fairly presents the accuracy concern, and the double transcription and audit in sentences (9) and (10) answer it, which makes the argument more credible. Acknowledging the concern does not mean the writer has given up the claim.$q$, 'draft', 'ae69533e-3a40-5e0c-9356-b6792fac88eb')
