   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence (11) as a conclusion that follows from the argument?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Volunteers are always better than professionals at every kind of archive work.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralizes"},{"text":"If the grant is denied again, the society should sell the ledgers to a university.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"History is important, and everyone should take time to visit their local museum.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"A checked volunteer project could make the mill ledgers searchable far sooner than one professional working alone, with accuracy close to a professional's and no grant required.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A checked volunteer project could make the mill ledgers searchable far sooner than one professional working alone, with accuracy close to a professional's and no grant required.$q$, $q$The correct conclusion ties the claim to the speed and accuracy evidence from Dorsey County. The claim that volunteers are always better overreaches, since the essay only shows their accuracy was close to a professional's.$q$, 'draft', 'ae69533e-3a40-5e0c-9356-b6792fac88eb')
