   $q$A reader suspects that the Brennick Conference canceled fewer practices in sentence (8) simply because last fall was cooler than usual. Which addition would best answer this doubt?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Cooler weather is common in some years and can make practices more pleasant.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"concedes-without-answer"},{"text":"Conference records show that the number of days above 90 degrees last fall was nearly the same as the year before.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Coaches in the conference said they were very pleased with how the season went.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"opinion-not-evidence"},{"text":"The conference plans to keep using the tiered system for at least three more years.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-to-doubt"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Conference records show that the number of days above 90 degrees last fall was nearly the same as the year before.$q$, $q$If the weather was about as hot as the previous year, the drop in cancellations is more likely due to the new system. Coaches' satisfaction is an opinion and says nothing about the temperatures.$q$, 'draft', '7f0cd155-6a0b-5ba4-a5c4-57de51c0cd9a')
