   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence (10) as the conclusion?$q$, $q$[{"text":"With donated equipment and existing disposal services, Linden Hall can keep a room that teaches science, planning and patience at a modest cost.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The school should also start a film club that meets on weekends.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"Art is a valuable part of every school, and students should take as many art classes as they can.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-general"},{"text":"Anyone who wants to turn the darkroom into a closet does not understand real photography.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dismissive-tone"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$With donated equipment and existing disposal services, Linden Hall can keep a room that teaches science, planning and patience at a modest cost.$q$, $q$The correct conclusion restates the claim and draws on both the benefits from paragraph one and the cost solutions from paragraph two. The weekend club adds a new proposal instead of closing the argument.$q$, 'draft', '242328e9-3dd5-568d-a0d2-763fe7f08981')
