insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('4f0cc545-43a3-5140-89ca-2f194f58e4a4', 'wg12-argument-writing-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-argument-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$A Wash Station for Lake Tarrow$q$, $q$(1) Lake Tarrow has so far remained free of invasive mussels, which have clogged water intakes and crowded out native species in at least six lakes within a day's drive. (2) The lake authority should require every boat entering from the public launch to pass through a free washing station during the summer season. (3) Mussel larvae are too small to see and can survive for several days in water left in a boat's motor, so a quick visual inspection cannot catch them. (4) At Pinecrest Reservoir, which installed a mandatory wash station eight years ago, regular surveys have found no mussels, while two unprotected lakes nearby became infested in the same period. (5) Removing mussels after they arrive costs far more than keeping them out; the town of Ellery spends about 140,000 dollars a year clearing its water intake pipes.

(6) Some anglers object that waiting for a wash will delay early morning launches, when fishing is best. (7) This objection matters, because a rule that people resent is a rule people will try to avoid. (8) The authority could open the station at 4:30 in the morning and add a second wash lane on weekends, when lines are longest. (9) With two lanes, the average wait at Pinecrest is under seven minutes.

(10) In the end, there are many lakes in the state, and all of them are special.$q$, 'draft')
on conflict (id) do update set title = excluded.title, body = excluded.body
