   $q$Read the sentence: "The archivists faced a difficult choice, restore the faded map or scan it exactly as it was." Which revision is punctuated correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The archivists faced a difficult choice. Restore the faded map or scan it exactly as it was.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unintended-command"},{"text":"The archivists faced a difficult choice: restore the faded map or scan it exactly as it was.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The archivists faced: a difficult choice, restore the faded map or scan it exactly as it was.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-after-verb"},{"text":"The archivists faced a difficult choice; restore the faded map or scan it exactly as it was.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-for-colon"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The archivists faced a difficult choice: restore the faded map or scan it exactly as it was.$q$, $q$The first clause is complete, and what follows spells out the choice, so a colon is the right mark. A semicolon or a period would cut the explanation off as a separate statement, so "restore the faded map" would read as a command to the reader instead of the choice the archivists faced.$q$, 'draft', null)
