   $q$Read the sentence: "The rowing club stored three small wooden boats in the boathouse." Which version punctuates the adjectives correctly?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The rowing club stored three small wooden, boats in the boathouse.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"comma-before-noun"},{"text":"The rowing club stored three small wooden boats in the boathouse.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The rowing club stored three small, wooden boats in the boathouse.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"commas-between-cumulative-adjectives"},{"text":"The rowing club stored three, small, wooden boats in the boathouse.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"commas-between-cumulative-adjectives"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The rowing club stored three small wooden boats in the boathouse.$q$, $q$"Three small wooden" are cumulative adjectives: each one builds on the next, and they cannot be reordered or joined with "and," so no commas are used. Separating them with commas treats them as coordinate adjectives by mistake.$q$, 'draft', null)
