   $q$Which sentence about the field station's water filter is punctuated correctly throughout?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The students built a well-designed, low cost water filter for the field station.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-compound-hyphen"},{"text":"The students built a well designed, low-cost water filter for the field station.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"missing-compound-hyphen"},{"text":"The students built a well-designed, low-cost-water filter for the field station.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"hyphen-joins-noun"},{"text":"The students built a well-designed, low-cost water filter for the field station.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The students built a well-designed, low-cost water filter for the field station.$q$, $q$"Well-designed" and "low-cost" are both compound adjectives before the noun phrase "water filter," so each is hyphenated, and the comma separates them as coordinate modifiers. Attaching "water" to "low-cost" wrongly folds part of the noun into the modifier.$q$, 'draft', null)
