   $q$Read the sentence: "The upholsterer will ___ the worn dining chairs with new striped fabric." Which choice correctly fills the blank to mean "cover again"?$q$, $q$[{"text":"re cover","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"open-compound-error"},{"text":"recover","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-similar-word"},{"text":"recover-","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"stray-hyphen"},{"text":"re-cover","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$re-cover$q$, $q$A hyphen after the prefix "re" is used when the solid word would be confused with a different word, so "re-cover" means "cover again." "Recover" means "get back" or "get well," which is not the meaning intended here.$q$, 'draft', null)
