   $q$Which sentence correctly introduces and punctuates the list of expedition members?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The expedition included: three specialists, Sven Aalto, a geologist; Priya Nair, a medic; and Kwame Asante, a photographer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"colon-after-verb"},{"text":"The expedition included three specialists: Sven Aalto, a geologist, Priya Nair, a medic, and Kwame Asante, a photographer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"commas-in-complex-series"},{"text":"The expedition included three specialists; Sven Aalto, a geologist; Priya Nair, a medic; and Kwame Asante, a photographer.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"semicolon-for-colon"},{"text":"The expedition included three specialists: Sven Aalto, a geologist; Priya Nair, a medic; and Kwame Asante, a photographer.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The expedition included three specialists: Sven Aalto, a geologist; Priya Nair, a medic; and Kwame Asante, a photographer.$q$, $q$A colon after the complete clause "The expedition included three specialists" introduces the list, and semicolons separate items that already contain commas. With commas only, the list could be read as six people instead of three.$q$, 'draft', null)
