   $q$Which sentence would best replace sentence 12 as the conclusion of the report?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The core drilled at Teller Ridge in 2021 was 2,400 meters long.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"restates-detail"},{"text":"Every government in the world should pay for many more ice cores right away.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-call-to-action"},{"text":"Ocean floor sediments can also be drilled to study the history of the seas.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"introduces-new-topic"},{"text":"Because they preserve both ancient air and a datable record of when it was sealed, ice cores let scientists compare today's atmosphere with that of the distant past.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Because they preserve both ancient air and a datable record of when it was sealed, ice cores let scientists compare today's atmosphere with that of the distant past.$q$, $q$The correct sentence draws together the trapping of air (paragraphs 1 and 2) and the dating of ice (paragraph 3) and states why the topic matters. The sentence about the core's length only repeats a detail from sentence 5.$q$, 'draft', '6914d92c-8813-5988-ae30-baed5619fd55')
