insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('d0501be2-285f-5383-a0c9-d1b5a53f9181', 'wg12-informative-writing-p02', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-informative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$The Stepwells of Kesara$q$, $q$(1) For centuries, communities on the semi-arid plains of Kesara faced a difficult pattern: heavy rain fell for about three months each year, and almost none fell during the other nine. (2) Their solution was the stepwell, a deep stone structure in which long flights of steps descend to a pool of groundwater. (3) Because the water level rose during the rainy season and dropped during the dry months, the steps allowed people to reach the water at any depth.

(4) The largest stepwell in the region, at the village of Ranakot, descends about thirty meters through nine levels. (5) Builders lined its walls with fitted sandstone blocks that kept the surrounding soil from collapsing into the shaft. (6) Shaded landings at each level also made the stepwell a cool gathering place, and records kept by local officials describe travelers resting there during the hottest part of the day.

(7) Many stepwells fell out of use in the late 1800s. (8) New pumps and piped water made it easier to draw water from deep wells, and some stepwells were filled with debris. (9) Others were neglected so long that their steps cracked and their pools became stagnant.

(10) In 2016, the Kesara Water Trust began restoring twelve stepwells. (11) Workers removed tons of silt and repaired the stone channels that once guided runoff into the pools. (12) Within three rainy seasons, the water level in nearby wells had risen by an average of two meters, according to the trust's monitoring reports. (13) The restored stepwells now serve as both reservoirs and public spaces for concerts and school visits.$q$, 'draft')
