   $q$Which sentence, added after sentence 13, would best support the limitation stated in sentence 12 with specific information?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The team hopes to repeat the study on a larger scale soon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"plan-not-evidence"},{"text":"A follow-up survey a year later found that only about a third of the extra fish remained on the playback patches.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Many scientists believe the experiment is extremely interesting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"vague-support"},{"text":"Coral reefs are found in warm, shallow waters around the world.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"off-focus-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$A follow-up survey a year later found that only about a third of the extra fish remained on the playback patches.$q$, $q$The follow-up figure gives measured evidence that the benefit may not last, which directly supports "limited." The plan to repeat the study is related, but it describes future intentions rather than evidence of a limitation.$q$, 'draft', '826cc092-a76a-51b9-8926-27ac2b2c98c8')
