   $q$Why is it important that sentence 3 appears early in the narrative?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It resolves the main conflict before the narrator ever steps into the creek.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-resolution"},{"text":"It introduces the narrator's partner so the reader knows who holds the net.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misplaces-character-introduction"},{"text":"It explains why the larvae matter, so the count in sentence 16 feels meaningful.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It describes the cold water so the reader can feel the narrator's discomfort.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-sensory-with-context"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It explains why the larvae matter, so the count in sentence 16 feels meaningful.$q$, $q$Without sentence 3, forty-one mayflies would just be a number; with it, the reader understands they signal a healthy creek. Jun is introduced in sentence 4, not sentence 3.$q$, 'draft', '45ab10b5-fea1-5c1f-9c7a-06ea5df02e70')
