-- Passage wg12-narrative-writing-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('aa203434-f8ac-5def-8443-f0a04b3b03ff', 'wg12-narrative-writing-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'write-g12-narrative-writing'), null,
        '9-12', $q$The Exchange Zone$q$, $q$(1) In a sprint relay, the baton must pass between runners inside a zone just thirty meters long, and a single fumble can end a race. (2) I ran the third leg for our team, which meant I received the baton on the curve and handed it to our anchor, Dominique Asante. (3) All season, our handoffs had been clumsy. (4) At the state qualifier, we dropped the baton in the final exchange and did not finish.

(5) Coach Ferreira changed our practices after that. (6) Every afternoon for two weeks, Dominique and I ran nothing but handoffs, sometimes forty in a row. (7) Dominique would start running when I reached a strip of tape on the track, and I would shout "Stick!" when I was close enough to place the baton in an open hand. (8) At first Dominique started too early and I could not catch up. (9) Then the start came too late and we nearly collided. (10) Slowly, we moved the tape until we found the right spot. (11) The track had been resurfaced the previous summer with a new rubber coating.

(12) It was the championship meet. (13) I came off the curve, saw the tape, and watched Dominique begin to run. (14) "Stick!" I shouted. (15) The baton smacked into an open palm, and Dominique was gone. (16) We finished second, our fastest time of the year.$q$, 'draft')
