   $q$A classmate suggests deleting sentence 4 to shorten the draft. Why should the writer keep it?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It provides sensory description of the track that helps the reader picture the setting.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-setting-with-cause"},{"text":"It gives the failure that causes the new practices and makes the clean handoff a redemption.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It is the only sentence that tells the reader which leg of the relay the narrator runs.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misattributes-detail"},{"text":"It contains the narrative's only dialogue, which the story needs to feel realistic.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misidentifies-dialogue"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It gives the failure that causes the new practices and makes the clean handoff a redemption.$q$, $q$Sentence 4 explains why Coach Ferreira changes practice in sentence 5 and why the final handoff matters so much. The narrator's leg is stated in sentence 2, not sentence 4.$q$, 'draft', 'aa203434-f8ac-5def-8443-f0a04b3b03ff')
