   $q$The writer considers deleting sentence 2 because it explains equipment instead of describing an event. What is the best advice?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Delete it, because a narrative should contain only actions and dialogue, never explanation.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"false-rule"},{"text":"Delete it, because the same information appears again in sentence 7.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-repetition"},{"text":"Keep it, because it gives the background readers need to grasp the jam and the falling skyline.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Keep it, but move it to the end so the narrative closes with technical information.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"weak-ending-placement"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Keep it, because it gives the background readers need to grasp the jam and the falling skyline.$q$, $q$Without sentence 2, a reader new to theater would not understand why a lock could stop the rope or why the backdrop drops so fast. Sentence 7 describes the lock, not how a line set works, so the information is not repeated.$q$, 'draft', 'b6d6c2f9-3e24-5625-927f-10feea480caf')
